// endpoint_roll_back_session.proto — RollBackSession: rewind the main agent's
// vendor conversation to just before one of its prompts, optionally restoring
// the files the agent's edit tools changed since then.
//
// One operation, run by the shim because the shim alone owns the vendor query:
//   1. The open turn, if any, is interrupted exactly as an unforced KillTurn
//      interrupts it.
//   2. `restore_files` only: every item of detached work (subagent, shell,
//      monitor, workflow) that a dropped turn spawned, transitively, is
//      stopped, and the files are restored to their state when the prompt was
//      sent (the vendor's file checkpointing; the shim runs every session with
//      it on).
//   3. The query is restarted on the same vendor session, resumed at the last
//      chain entry before the prompt, so the vendor's own conversation no
//      longer holds the prompt or anything after it.
//
// THE PROMPT'S VENDOR IDENTITY IS DERIVED FROM ITS TURN ID. The shim sends each
// prompt under a vendor message uuid computed from the turn id the daemon
// minted (a turn id that is itself a uuid — a prompt the vendor recorded
// first — is its own vendor uuid), so a restarted shim finds the prompt's
// record in the vendor transcript with nothing stored anywhere.
//
// Nothing is retried. A cut the vendor refuses leaves the conversation whole:
// the shim resumes the session plainly and answers the refusal.

